  "meta": {
    "comment": "Phase-3 tribulation table (ROADMAP 'Tribulations'). One entry per realm id — the canonical 15-tier DESIGN.md ladder, in tier order — consumed by the TribulationSystem (js/systems/tribulations.js): tribulationType is the realm's tribulation (null = the realm imposes no tribulation gate; otherwise one of the canonical DESIGN.md types), and results is the weighted outcome table faced when the pending tribulation is resolved. Canonical outcomes: survived, barely-survived (SUCCESS — the gate opens), injured (progressLoss 0.5), near-death (progressLoss 1) (FAILURE — progress is lost and the gate stays pending). Death is excluded in v1 — DESIGN.md marks it 'future optional' (same discipline as breakthroughs). Per-realm success weight is ~80% and failure ~20% (placeholder balancing — Phase 10 Balancing retunes)."
  },
